WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.703
-My next guest is known as
the queen of Latin pop,

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.238
and she has a brand-new album

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.340
out this Friday called
"Desamorfosis."

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.209
Please welcome Thalia!

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:11.744
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:15.882
Oh, my goodness!
Look at this! Come on!

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.251
-Jimmy, mi amor!

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.719
-I'm so happy that you're here,
number one.

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:21.921
Number two, thank you

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:24.457
for premiering your video
tonight for "Mojito."

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.692
It's a big deal,
and we love that.

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.027
Thank you very much.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:30.963
-Oh, my God, I'm so excited
about this.

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:32.464
Thank you for having me here.

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:36.935
-How is the family? How is
Tommy doing, your husband?

00:00:36.935 --> 00:00:40.540
-Tommy, you know, he's always
busy, always working.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.175
He has like three projects
right now.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.810
You probably know all about it

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.578
because you guys talk
all the time.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.646
-Tommy Mottola is your husband.
-Exciting.

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:50.883
-How did you and Tommy meet?
Do you remember?

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:54.620
-Oh, my --
Okay, this was a blind date,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.056
and it was
Gloria and Emilio Estefan

00:00:57.056 --> 00:01:00.426
that kept telling us,
"You know what?"

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:03.329
Emilio kept saying, "Thalia,
you have to meet this guy.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.398
You have to meet this guy.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.267
He's like you.
He thinks like you."

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.603
And I kept asking him,
"Okay, but tell me --

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.705
tell me about this guy,
what he does."

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.908
"He just got divorced.
He has two kids."

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.010
And I'm like, "No thank you."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.712
"I'm free right now.
I feel very good right now."

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:23.183
And he kept telling Tommy
the same like,

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.551
"You have to meet this girl.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:28.654
I mean, you guys are like --
like so alike."

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.557
And then Tommy's like, "Okay,
but tell me what she does.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:32.792
Tell me about her."

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.927
-[ Laughs ] My God,
that's a good impression.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:38.097
-And then he's like,
"Okay, she's an actress,

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.832
and she's a singer,"
and Tommy was like,

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.066
"Nope, thank you very much."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:43.936
-Oh, my gosh. That's hilarious.
-"That's it."

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:48.741
One year and a half,
after we met at Scalinatella --

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.177
you probably love that story,
because you like to eat like me.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.447
-I love Scalinatella.
-And from that day till now,

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.783
20-plus years,
two kids, gorgeous kids.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:01.421
-Come on. Look at that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:05.124
I've seen photos of your
wedding, 'cause it was --

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:08.293
I mean, everyone who was anyone
was at your wedding.

00:02:08.293 --> 00:02:10.696
I mean, it was insane.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:13.699
-It was really something.

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:15.368
It was insane.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:22.108
It was, you know, the Mexicans
and the Italians,

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.143
and then New York scene,

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:25.845
and then it was,
like, mariachi band,

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.847
and then it was a big band.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:31.217
And then at the end of
the night -- I don't know how --

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.486
up on stage,
it was Donna Summer,

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:37.389
Gloria Estefan, Marc Anthony.

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:40.560
Danny DeVito was, like, dancing.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.595
-I love how Danny DeVito got
the biggest round of applause.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.196
-Hold on. Pero hold on.

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:47.433
He was dancing,
holding on Jennifer Lopez waist.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.102
He's not stupid.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:51.304
He is not stupid.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.906
He was doing the conga
with Jennifer.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.074
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.610
Jennifer was so happy,
and he was like, "Yeah!"

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.612
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.348
A lot of tequila.
A lot of tequila that night.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.950
-Yeah. Good, good, good.
[ Applause ]

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.452
I want to talk about
"Desamorfosis,"

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.789
but first, I wanted to mention
that, at one point,

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.424
some of your songs were banned
at one point,

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:14.293
when you first came out.
-Yes. Yes.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:18.731
-Because they were too racy
or what was it?

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.133
-They were, like, very,
you know, a lot of, like,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:25.070
sexual content and a lot
of very explicit things,

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.407
and about concepts that back
then probably were, like,

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:31.978
too much for, like,
a 17-year-old girl.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.981
And they banned me on radio.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:39.051
And 30 years after, right now,

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.621
we just released
the same albums,

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:44.523
my first three solo albums,
digitally,

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:48.260
and they were like number one,
two, three -- They're top five.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.295
-Yeah. The top --
-In the digital era.

00:03:50.295 --> 00:03:51.397
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.798
They come out now.
That's got to feel good.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:53.966
[ Cheers and applause ]
See?

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:56.702
-I'm like, "Yes!"
-Well, you have a new album.

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:59.371
It comes out this Friday,
"Desamorfosis."

00:03:59.371 --> 00:04:01.941
What can people expect
from this album?

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:04.243
-First of all,
that sounds so good.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.512
"Desamorfosis."
That sounds great.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.881
-I did okay? "Desamorfosis."

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.417
-Yeah. "Desamorfosis."

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.520
"Desamorfosis."
-"Desamorfosis."

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.423
"Desamorfosis."
-Yes!

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.759
-Thank you. You have to help me,
Thalia, please.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:23.629
-You did good. So, "desamor"
means "heartbreak."

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.231
Okay?
"Amor" is "love," of course.

00:04:26.231 --> 00:04:28.501
"Morphosis" is "morfosis."

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.071
It's like a play on three words.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.805
And that's what love is.

00:04:33.805 --> 00:04:35.308
Love is an adventure.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:38.978
And it has all this complexity
of what love is.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.713
And it's a very honest album.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:46.252
I talk about all my things
there from beginning to end.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.621
And it's the first time
that I did this.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.457
It's like going to therapy,
and it was amazing.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.791
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:56.128
-I love there's a song on here
called "Tick Tock,"

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:59.898
because you have
a giant following on TikTok.

00:04:59.898 --> 00:05:04.937
And it's funny
because some generations

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.640
watch you on TikTok, and they
know you only from TikTok.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:11.911
-Yeah, they think I'm a TikToker
or, like, I'm a YouTuber

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.480
or, like, I'm an influencer.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.949
And then they discover,
when they Google me,

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.518
"Oh, my gosh, she's sings?"

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.152
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.954
-Oh, my God. I mean, come on.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.723
Exactly, like, "What?"

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.024
-It's really cool.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:28.360
And my fans, Jimmy, my fans
from all over,

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.698
they send me -- they tag me
and they DM me all the time

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:35.234
like, "You know what? There's
a new singer here in Brazil.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:39.004
You have to know all about her.
You and her would be amazing."

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:42.475
Or my fans from Greece --
"This is the new video director.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:44.510
Look at what he's doing.
You have to work."

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.111
So they're always tagging me,

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:49.048
and that's how I find
my collabs lately.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:52.385
You know, I just DM them.
"Hey, I love your music."

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:55.855
And they're like,
"A-Are you the Thalia? Are you?"

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.591
-They're like, "Really? Is this
really coming from Thalia?"

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:01.560
Yeah. Look at you. I love it.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.530
And then, I want to talk about
"Mojito," because I think

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.866
this is a perfect summer jam,

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.135
not only is it
the perfect summer beverage.

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:11.103
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:13.039
Why is it called "Mojito"?

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.174
-Well, it is like a very --

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.743
First of all,
the song is super sexy.

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:22.314
It has real music that,
to me, was important.

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:26.085
You know, it has, like,
the guitar and the bongos,

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.120
and the lyrics are like
what you said.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.422
It's like the perfect
summer song.

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:34.560
It's refreshing.
It's like mint, sugar, bubbles.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.230
-Yes!
-Kisses, lips, and oh!

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.698
-Yes!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:41.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.336
You are unbelievable. Thalia!

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:47.407
Her new album "Desamorfosis"
is out this Friday.

